From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 34/34] coherent: writes reach held batches past later command
 buffers; no waits on held records

- Records carry their part end and publish per completed batch (completing_parts);
  failed command buffers drop their records and leave the planned set.
- A later command buffer's take keeps the guest area and snapshots for a held batch
  (held_guest/held_snapshots); the join no longer drops a missing side (joined, not bounding).
  Done records merge into the pages before the stash.
- Held batches with no record are seen through late_waiters.
- Encoder takes and reader copy backs never wait on a record held for an event
  (wait_settled skip_held); host readers still wait, bounded.
- A reader whose commit-time copy back was not made copies back at its planning
  (copy_back_at_plan, from atlas/coh-d-lane3 f5239ecf); a plan-time copy back is left
  where stashed snapshots hold CPU writes.
- An ordered take passes over a write count only when Beside kept every write (plain).
- done records stay bounded (join of records no copy back left behind).
- Exit guard: host image copy entry points and the image read inside the guard.
- Lanes: 5 new held-batch lanes; reproductions un-ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
